  "caption": "Quinn's friend called reformer Pilates \"magic\" for back pain. Quinn's first class was a pro-level group, and the next morning the back was grumpier than ever.\n\nReformer Pilates can help ongoing low back pain, but the evidence suggests it isn't clearly better than other structured exercise. It's not a magic fix, and the best option is often the one you'll keep doing.\n\nWhat can help: picking a class you enjoy, telling the instructor about your back, starting with smaller beginner groups, judging each session by how you feel the next morning, and adding strength work if you've been inactive.\n\nGet an individual assessment first if symptoms are mostly in the leg, you're in a recent flare, or certain positions make the pain worse.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
